that are used to produce crops, they're used for humans-

01:23:46.073 --> 01:23:48.230
They're going everywhere.
Everywhere.

01:23:48.230 --> 01:23:50.286
And most of the crops anyway

01:23:50.286 --> 01:23:53.170
are growing food for the animals.

01:23:53.170 --> 01:23:54.170
Yeah, exactly.

01:23:54.170 --> 01:23:57.560
They hay, straw, barley types of grass

01:23:57.560 --> 01:24:00.280
for animals and animal product production.

01:24:00.280 --> 01:24:02.500
So it's kind of, again, a non-starter in the sense of,

01:24:02.500 --> 01:24:04.500
yes, of course, farmers will kill these mice

01:24:04.500 --> 01:24:05.810
when they're trying to protect

01:24:05.810 --> 01:24:07.520
the food they've grown directly for humans,

01:24:07.520 --> 01:24:09.600
but the problem exists for feed

01:24:09.600 --> 01:24:11.600
and crops being produced for animals

01:24:11.600 --> 01:24:14.010
and more of that land is being used for animals.

01:24:14.010 --> 01:24:15.010
So more mice have been killed

01:24:15.010 --> 01:24:17.370
for the animal production in the first place anyway.

01:24:17.370 --> 01:24:18.450
Yeah.

